{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.CategoricalReeb.ofWeightDecomposition","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.CategoricalReeb.ofWeightDecomposition","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalReeb.ofWeightDecomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalReeb.ofWeightDecomposition","kind":"def","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/CategoricalReeb/ofWeightDecomposition.lean#L27-L41","doc":"**Categorical Reeb normalisation** (named conditional conjecture).\n\nFor a categorical object `A` equipped with a Reeb endomorphism\n`ξ : A → A` and a contact 1-form `Θ_A : A → ℝ` (the scalar evaluation of\n`Θ_A : A → 𝟙`), `ofWeightDecomposition ξ Θ_A` is the proposition that the\n**normalisation** condition\n\n`∀ x, Θ_A (ξ x) = 1`     (categorically `Θ_A ∘ ξ = id_𝟙`)\n\nholds.  This names the conditional claim of the categorical-Reeb\nexistence proposition (pattern C); it is *not* asserted — an inhabitant\nwitnesses the Reeb-derivation normalisation. ","signatureChunk":0}]}